> Hee.  That leads me to the pop quiz up above.  I don't really care to
> risk it, but I thought it'd be interesting.  Maybe the stair placement
> code would plop me right back on my farming square, across the level
> from the stairs, right next to the altar, or maybe it would do an
> emergency shove, I don't know.  What's the code have to say?

If I remember correctly (but it's a while since I tried this so I may be 
misremembering):

The stair code will put you on top of something like a boulder if it has 
to.

If you leave the level with a single space and chase something up/down the 
stairs then when you return to the level you get precedence over the 
monsters and any monsters which cannot be placed simply disappear.

If you polymorph into a phasing creature, completely fill every single 
space on the level then teleport out, when you return the dungeon will 
collapse.


